on templates, graveyard UI, collector load-testing.\n\n**Test run: blocked, not skipped lightly.** The instruction was to run `pytest` including the 12 new tests — but this environment has no Python at all: `python`/`python3`/`py` are all absent from PATH, no venvs exist in the repo, and installing toolchains is out of scope for the sandbox. So there is no local verification output to quote; the 13-test file plus the existing suite gate must run in CI. The tests were written to the suite's existing conventions (pytest classes, direct module imports, temp-store isolation) to make that pass likely, but that is an inference, not a result.\n\n**Push: blocked on credentials (unchanged).** `git push origin feature/living-fleet-wiring` fails with `schannel: AcquireCredentialsHandle failed (SEC_E_NO_CREDENTIALS)` — the sandbox user cannot reach the Windows credential store behind `credential.helper=manager`, and no `gh`/`ssh`/tokens exist here. All 7 commits (4 from the prior run + 3 this run) are local. From your shell:\n\n```\ngit push -u origin feature/living-fleet-wiring\n```","provider_item_id":"msg_01a165acb8747519a30d8b9dac2d6d25","phase":"final_answer"}","truncated":false}
